{"id": "clm:87c2f956562942681e84694cdf021eb557cf8f68c92ba5082cda8a745c045ecd", "type": "statement", "text": "A neuropathy review describes multiple potential contributors in people with PD, including genetic disorders, treatment effects and concomitant disease; its diagnostic approach includes history, clinical examination, blood tests and nerve-conduction studies. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7847250/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:764aac4d3644c0b8fefe3d0b318aa60a0e2dbc4c923dc1df8720c0d2c674a5b8", "ev:b64593732d985086cd511d3e868ab79ee4762cd2f9be68972831dfdb36e460d0"]}
{"id": "clm:445ffdc44b74ab10b3dfc7479154d2d14fb14bafd313d0d37960ef50d2ed7def", "type": "statement", "text": "PD fatigue is a subjective lack of energy that interferes with function; it differs from sleepiness and from objectively measured muscle fatigability. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4883681/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.parkinson.org/library/fact-sheets/fatigue", "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10473113/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2e91964701383d82276fd5dc0373cd015b073cb132bf432e9fdd0aa80b1ce0f0", "ev:43ca37a315e822278b1481cd1ab2c55573e6773ac5b9a49271178fc8d57129fa", "ev:893dc156837db4b40cd0e57011b84c6f6677780572d6a337ddb2b677d7047a27"]}
{"id": "clm:4c55c94882b4f8da7673c0d02d79568612e3ac1ac4803b3dff16ea8275d0647c", "type": "statement", "text": "A review of Parkinson-related peripheral neuropathy lists diabetes, thyroid disease and B12 deficiency among acquired causes; sensory complaints therefore warrant assessment for peripheral neuropathy rather than automatic attribution to central PD pathology. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7847250/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7adecd31203da877688061677ac208cac13cc1fce62c1a571bafa09f7e173aea", "ev:f8d154cc14d1f4f1d3ae58d8d051c7673a4af4f6cb354a444574a5272a1c9aaa"]}
{"id": "clm:b71cb25a044068dad7adb57a4b2f03827fb65a73713119def6976f394d9239bc", "type": "statement", "text": "Rotigotine showed numerical pain improvement in an exploratory placebo-controlled pilot, but the primary pain comparison was not statistically significant; MDS classified its PD pain use as investigational rather than established efficacy. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26626320/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:15313354d7801553a777d5f7aa85b87512eb2a16517688828d02d6fde1a3d3e5", "ev:35fcb6728399d098d1b10e48d9f34a7603033cfbeb493bc11a82b7e8a4095823", "ev:5bd819ef8fca18480d7d1d5cd654d830e24047edbba44a27ffb40d17f94214e1", "ev:67669fad0ac2f93254c44d68b7e0def1464edaf7cfe0ffdb8a6a1069e2d13ee0"]}
{"id": "clm:be9d99f13130214100f4be5414db8fce5b9c37a6dbcb34485fc3ccb11d8e8abf", "type": "statement", "text": "A single-center sham-controlled trial of motor-cortex repetitive transcranial magnetic stimulation reported a favorable musculoskeletal-pain signal in PD; its small sample and short follow-up support a preliminary adjunctive-treatment claim rather than broad efficacy across PD pain types. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32980772/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:042503a958716657aeb4f5b8b4eb5283ce29ed6134a5efede37c3e5b157853ed", "ev:4b5f2783f7ff8441a0d882fab5bfcf358fbd37c4d2066d41de7e8e117fa2555a", "ev:54f55f2ac13b3acc190a901eb9d2f0d66565f720a8cda1f015dc77cc4114973b", "ev:7c072a106f6d3076f074f2a13a5e4c4c72d733596d81365565847bb678f8e8a3"]}
{"id": "clm:20dce067f1f4f41a4a86f58b8ffab2354f9687c5fc75cab986fdde7ce60a49ae", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2020 pain review distinguishes musculoskeletal, dystonic, nerve, primary and akathitic pain in PD; the heterogeneous pain presentation supports syndrome-specific assessment rather than a single analgesic strategy. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2035-8377/12/3/14", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5e48bbd128b18b13dfc04c9df635f5138495ed1411987a50b37680182ccf4c97", "ev:616357fe3cd2a8e5b123c178d54cfb469823659f829dca851cfd1cbd19234b31", "ev:e56b9f8745d7e57829a47fe6ac7a19ca7383f45e7551475ecb3d3a3424d4bc82"]}
{"id": "clm:49704caa87ed230a6ec39ff7a7d1706c31d7f642d36cc7671eee47021ecb1926", "type": "statement", "text": "A 2023 systematic review searching trials through May 2021 found a small fatigue benefit from physical exercise across eight trials, but called for further efficacy research and differentiation of physical versus mental fatigue outcomes. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10473113/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:32de7b3ce299af39cf4bc6b1bc67526a691daaed27a12b134d2e50125fd3d7fd", "ev:569a0a580110aa9d6d60235391ba9707c6f76f2739c2bf4153a6653ac0644898", "ev:8d7997453db1daab946cfe39880ac1eb9ca196072b95fb3519c7e085e781cac8", "ev:a616c94073b6770c481d45bf9d27ea62464fe207a9a784f2a28a7298aaf541e3"]}
{"id": "clm:fa45f9b098c4cc7992c07ea886e856f40ed7430d6d1f8217be7e0e739f0f49d8", "type": "statement", "text": "In that 2023 review, pooled modafinil trials did not show a significant fatigue benefit versus placebo, and acupuncture did not show a significant advantage over sham acupuncture; these comparisons should not be presented as proven PD-fatigue therapies. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10473113/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:16f4127df6f5587bb61728dfbd3e4eabcac82eb74e28707a00eb76ba70b0ad5e", "ev:32de7b3ce299af39cf4bc6b1bc67526a691daaed27a12b134d2e50125fd3d7fd", "ev:703a053f07837720b06024b248d79b70954d68910eef18c7f319fe024550ff66", "ev:8f94e7c6d76bdfa8c0c069766e9efaab02e72db9d5f757aee8d954669c9256e7"]}
{"id": "clm:7800ff48021e467716a3e4120ec357d7c561b05bb743d2720fb57f59e8317fa2", "type": "statement", "text": "Sensory symptoms in PD extend beyond pain: a 2023 review describes disturbances of vision, hearing, smell, taste, touch, temperature and position sense. This review-level observation does not establish a specific treatment for each disturbance. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37258441/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:417e88303a90c88082b282f7307fac555f043f01c2c111415b5f732c57e093eb", "ev:71dd5bc155f01fbe3d7854729f2af9eac66f2da39848706469cbc7c6e3a5126f", "ev:9a99314f228dab4247599285eb04c1732d707aae1ccee29429e5d214555fa242"]}
{"id": "clm:048f4d8619c86adad3d948c3f4aed22626b2111b460eaa09ce3b4fa2c6242eb2", "type": "statement", "text": "For fatigue, the 2019 MDS review classified methylphenidate and modafinil as investigational with insufficient evidence; the Foundation likewise notes that the small positive methylphenidate trial needs further study. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.parkinson.org/library/fact-sheets/fatigue"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3f93107b2208d5c1b73b683cb866089dca482fb49dc16dd739f86f10b69faa33", "ev:5284acaeb9d5ef2b1bc93c3868b60fb40d8ad4ff1e95e7bc3fb8697f290220a5", "ev:bcb00ee98eec707ce50be03771fe1da19640942a9f7c4958f1daba0aa5d9c7de", "ev:cabed6e45e9fa8495c8d572ebf52f98e7baf9a0b71bd80a4eb46fa24aa5be668"]}
{"id": "clm:2a8540c211ac19e16c3f1681af41c82d6293547acf465699b35285ab11a3cbb7", "type": "statement", "text": "PANDA did not meet its primary pain endpoint at week 16. The 2019 MDS review accordingly found insufficient efficacy evidence for prolonged-release oxycodone–naloxone, despite a possibly useful practice rating based partly on its use for severe chronic pain outside PD. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26494524/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:00b3f40a198102ee38c6284624474d55ad080e49d8749514be9a58beb536dc47", "ev:3f93107b2208d5c1b73b683cb866089dca482fb49dc16dd739f86f10b69faa33", "ev:73b9b42d7ea8ae7dc2596f1784aa0a18855ee3a918c007bd8fca38dad24c7bc9", "ev:9bc79eea345c2d4b89c85e57916dbf511b53ae9504ba1e70e2bf04fcb42135d3", "ev:f15ffe45d7b35babb378dc3a3630fb54a7fa81f2c531e9455453b8bbf2f6cd22"]}
{"id": "clm:8fc6d105f0f57472e4b77ec4f8e626b989831ccaf924269ebecf039e31435306", "type": "statement", "text": "In the 2024 OXYDOPA trial in parkinsonian central pain, neither prolonged-release oxycodone nor higher-dose levodopa demonstrated superiority over placebo. Adverse events leading to discontinuation were more frequent with oxycodone; the finding applies to this central-pain population. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38850081/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:44a05216eb35b13e2456e73a682040a1554916e9f81e4358d17f10b8ed921f13", "ev:abb2af275aa3f017a5196c37e0bdaf242ddead6f9a080e1c110e516fbba95439", "ev:beffd3d6343c007c075e048d02e3f1200f9cf575c073aa4e1ef58658d836a74b", "ev:e64260f56859047409e3c86ad82f83e4566f62b7f5e3ca7b462ed10fa99ee784"]}
{"id": "clm:cdde1bcf37d67a543d635d2ccbae96eb8bcafd6d9b1a3a4c7e69b4cd57fd770b", "type": "statement", "text": "Real acupuncture did not outperform sham acupuncture for PD fatigue in the Kluger and Kong randomized trials; a 2026 review likewise characterized fatigue evidence as very uncertain and without superiority over sham. Within-group improvement should not be presented as treatment-specific efficacy. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27028133/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5853635/", "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13189933/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:109d155df88b5d01c3e4c472d3e087c66aef0dfaa5fb34c09019e51719c80a63", "ev:2f36d964f2c30d88d094ab89d9cbbcc60599a0c51513ee56cba63924416bc962", "ev:69f0949914992c0f75de3dc3c058cf04758eb11e9eca456e058aad8d8dee6344", "ev:83d514ad3bd50f7a58f516f808ae23c103692672454e0b7f917e66e0abc27e76", "ev:8addbded30821b666dffbe6a8c29671daa65b05ea40be6b2a36b094dce109652", "ev:c434fa17a81e5e16e6eea7ea0dea4010e57c5dfd5cad3eb60baf8dcbfdf26b56", "ev:d52d2d25b49bc042fae7c2028506b1f31cdada63e97d011c9604708bc3dcc95e", "ev:fd7fe316ae15c77f7567bd38dbaa62f1ca4f9c07e79d5ee78e0b3519305b04ab"]}
{"id": "clm:4948c9f44dbc77ae9ade23cdbf6839211e8e2b2d149085131862a93e4a9439f3", "type": "statement", "text": "Small experimental studies found that levodopa can increase pain thresholds in PD. These laboratory threshold results should be distinguished from demonstrated relief of chronic clinical pain. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16078219/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2117570/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:88db2cbe81eb49bae1d73ac48bd04e89560bc1a71541a679e54efd001d62f4ac", "ev:92e5206c01e349d2f63e5295737a5b5c193c0570cfdfe11e18e5dab63af31661", "ev:b96d308434bee2fa275d0cae119209dccb450db6ed900a43a466650a743df7ec", "ev:ef0df5a5c9a054b8a64f9d5ee39e3a760cc7298c6f6570880f710eec8dd4b079"]}
{"id": "clm:d5081c12228976d7f05352b391fbc10401461e79884d56b0f4ac5443def15c87", "type": "statement", "text": "Experimental findings on sensory thresholds conflict: one study reported that thermal and mechanical pain thresholds were uninfluenced by levodopa or STN-DBS, whereas another reported significant increases in mechanical pain and tolerance thresholds after acute STN-DBS and after acute levodopa administration. A uniform direct effect on central pain processing is not established by these studies. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20629160/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23864314/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:01b54a5d42314bb1f4dc7a0944868c20c2ee435388dc43e8789f5051261ab049", "ev:526a7e788cb43c9127929d522158776d0f273ed180f5458f8e9f4730d0f4e60a"]}
{"id": "clm:6fec430cce4d2db789d35be013ef0b01c62d8c574b7c33e9624490b7a748a41a", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2020 review describes musculoskeletal pain associated with postural changes and muscular rigidity, including frozen shoulder, low back pain, arthritis and osteoporosis. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2035-8377/12/3/14", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:98390c9cab62edc84982b36356dc6fb9bff48b27dba52564fa8d3d0254e078f8", "ev:e56b9f8745d7e57829a47fe6ac7a19ca7383f45e7551475ecb3d3a3424d4bc82"]}
{"id": "clm:c539cb73b826c6ba71aecc84e05881a41949bcde87d9291705c058c602f7dc11", "type": "statement", "text": "In the 2015 PANDA trial, prolonged-release oxycodone-naloxone did not meet the primary pain endpoint in the full analysis population at week 16; the authors nevertheless considered the signal worthy of further research. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26494524/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:33a2bdbbb64fd7b769745006e9d4a729b828ccde1bdfa8594661e865f4cba207", "ev:fd0c246a68cfa4682a47822c5686fc9e7f8f1fb00595979e316cf6ac29ae9fa6"]}
{"id": "clm:6305a52fda564e001846b8b070825bc50129f5be4216e2bdec268867fb34b159", "type": "statement", "text": "Sensory symptoms include diminished smell, which can precede PD diagnosis; the Parkinson’s Foundation notes that reduced smell can also reduce enjoyment of food and appetite. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)", "source_url": "https://www.parkinson.org/understanding-parkinsons/non-movement-symptoms", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD pain, fatigue and sensory symptoms"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:b910e8016c1651674ba32b00149e6c40a24df2c32f7ad4267bb63084380a5417", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0c2d66985719e8659c048e807b46e77672239eaaaa3dc7dd0dc25fed0daa3464", "ev:91c0348ba0ac3276a13c6075ec1ca6f613bc8d02b2e9f212f904184ed30cc18d"]}
